# webgl-virgl.flakes: the subtests of WebGL pages that judge.py webgl does
# not judge in the virgl cases, `PATH ERE` a line, PATH as the suite's list
# gives it and ERE an extended regular expression searched for in the
# subtest's message.
#
# occlusion-query-scissor.html: an ANY_SAMPLES_PASSED query whose draws a
# 0x0 scissor rectangle leaves empty reads 1 in 53 to 64 of the page's 65
# such passes, which ones changing from run to run, in both browsers in the
# Debian guest as on Rach2 (dev-log/84-locks/upstream.md); the page's 454
# other subtests passed in every run and are judged.
conformance2/query/occlusion-query-scissor.html ^pass [0-9]+, result: 1 === expected: 0$
#
# fboinvalidate/whole.html and target.html in Chromium's chunk 3: from
# fbocolorbuffer/tex3d_01.html on, the host's virglrenderer has refused
# Chromium's context ("context error reported", GL error 1281, then "Illegal
# command buffer") and every case reads back an image it did not draw, its
# difference thousands against the threshold's 0.05. Which cases pass by
# chance changes from run to run in the Debian guest: its reference failed
# 18 and 23 of their cases, and a run on 2026-11-15 failed 19 and 27 twice,
# as Rach2 does (dev-log/84-locks/84-265s.md).
deqp/functional/gles3/fboinvalidate/whole.html ^invalidate\.whole\.
deqp/functional/gles3/fboinvalidate/target.html ^invalidate\.target\.
